# PublicDeliveryFormation v1

A formation is customer-specific, provider-neutral, and contains no provider client, shell invocation, SDK, raw secret, or ambient deployment authority. A typed OpaqueSecretReference may identify provider-held custody but never carries secret values.

PublicDeliverySolicitation(formationType=PublicDeliveryFormation, customer, formationDigest, artifactDigest, targetDigest, executionMode, exactEffects)
  -> ProviderExactEffectOffer(author=provider, same formation/artifact/target/effects)
  -> CustomerOfferAcceptance(author=customer, offerDigest, same formation/artifact/target)
  -> CustodyGrantReference(grantDigest, same formation/artifact/target)
  -> DigestBoundArtifact(attestationDigest, same formation/artifact/target)
  -> ProviderEffectReceipt(receiptDigest, artifactAttestationDigest, nonempty closed residue vector, same formation/artifact/target)
  -> IndependentExternalAssay(independent=true, stage=staging, passed=true, artifactAttestationDigest, effectReceiptDigest, same formation/artifact/target)
  -> CutoverAdmission.

Every stage closes before its successor. Malformed, unbound, secret-bearing, or open input settles as a typed DeploymentFormationRefusal at its seam. A dry run can claim packaging or planning only; it cannot claim authority, DNS, runtime actuation, deployment, publication, upload, serving, routing, headers, access policy, TLS, rollback, or cutover. Receipt residue dimensions are artifactByteParity, requestedProviderRoute, effectScopeAndCustody, dnsTlsPath, accessPolicy, and rollback; each is pass, fail, not-claimed, or not-applicable. Required residues are nonempty and delivery is true only when every one is pass. Cutover admits only after artifact-attested staging, a delivered provider receipt, and an independent assay bound to the same formation, artifact, target, attestation, and effect receipt.
